// workspace_topology.proto — HOW A NEW WORKSPACE STANDS TO OTHER WORK: its
// relationship to its creator's work, the branch it is cut from and lands in,
// and the conversation it starts with. Shared by every rpc that makes a
// workspace (CreateWorkspace, in each of its forms) or moves one
// (SetWorkspaceParent).
//
// THREE INDEPENDENT CHOICES. A create names its relationship (child or peer),
// its context origin, and, where the relationship's default is not wanted, its
// landing target. They answer different questions: whom the workspace
// coordinates with, where its work goes, and what it already knows.
//
// THE OWNERSHIP RULE, which the landing-target arms make structural: a branch
// cut from the primary branch lands only on the primary branch, and a branch
// cut from a workspace's branch lands only into that workspace. The one way
// work on a branch no workspace owns reaches anything is the async merge
// (CreateWorkspaceAsyncMerge), whose source and target are its own.

